Package: mappingAS
Type: Package
Title: Spatial Metrics and Habitat Conversion for Extinction Risk Assessment
Version: 1.3.2
Authors@R: 
    person("Antônio Lucas Barreira Rodrigues", email = "barreira_rodrigues@hotmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a spatial analytical framework for species extinction 
    risk assessment following the IUCN Red List Criterion B guidelines. 
    Computes the Extent of Occurrence (EOO) and Area of Occupancy (AOO) 
    from occurrence data and integrates land-use and land-cover (LULC) 
    data to quantify habitat loss, It also integrates MapBiomas Fire data 
    to compute cumulative burned areas and fire recurrence timeseries. 
    The package leverages MapBiomas collections to calculate the proportion 
    of anthropic conversion within range metrics. It supports both local 
    high-resolution raster processing and cloud-based computation via 
    Google Earth Engine (GEE) for large-scale assessments. An interactive 
    'shiny' application is included to facilitate reproducible workflows in conservation planning.
